{:theorem
 {:id :theorem,
  :statement
  "Let $A$ be a Hermitian operator and $U = U_1 \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes U_n$ be a product of single-qubit unitaries. Then $\\mathrm{Inf}(U A U^\\dagger) = \\mathrm{Inf}(A)$.",
  :content-hash "d577c91ff4242c0a"},
 :obligations [],
 :archived-nodes {},
 :external-refs {},
 :nodes
 {:1-l5a001
  {:statement
   "Recall the quantum influence of $A$ is defined as $\\mathrm{Inf}(A) = \\sum_{P \\in \\mathcal{P}_n} \\mathrm{wt}(P) \\cdot \\pi_A(P) = \\mathbb{E}_{P \\sim \\pi_A}[\\mathrm{wt}(P)]$ where $\\pi_A(P) = \\frac{\\hat{a}(P)^2}{\\|A\\|_2^2}$ is the Pauli spectral distribution and $\\mathrm{wt}(P) = |\\{i : P_i \\neq I\\}|$ is the weight.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "a5e34657540958d3",
   :display-order 1,
   :type :definition,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :definition-expansion,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-l5a001,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{}},
  :1-l5a002
  {:statement
   "For any single-qubit unitary $V$, conjugation maps the Pauli group to itself (up to phases): $V I V^\\dagger = I$ and $V P V^\\dagger \\in \\{\\pm X, \\pm Y, \\pm Z, \\pm iX, \\pm iY, \\pm iZ\\}$ for $P \\in \\{X, Y, Z\\}$. In particular, $\\mathrm{wt}(V P V^\\dagger) = \\mathrm{wt}(P)$ for any single-qubit Pauli $P$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "999b1c155aa9abda",
   :display-order 2,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :algebraic-rewrite,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-l5a002,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{}},
  :1-l5a003
  {:statement
   "For a product unitary $U = U_1 \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes U_n$ and Pauli string $P = P_1 \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes P_n$, we have $U P U^\\dagger = (U_1 P_1 U_1^\\dagger) \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes (U_n P_n U_n^\\dagger)$. Since each $U_i P_i U_i^\\dagger$ has the same weight contribution as $P_i$ (either 0 for $I$ or 1 for non-$I$), we have $\\mathrm{wt}(U P U^\\dagger) = \\sum_i \\mathbf{1}[P_i \\neq I] = \\mathrm{wt}(P)$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "3eb5caf98eb6c59f",
   :display-order 3,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :algebraic-rewrite,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-l5a003,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{:1-l5a002}},
  :1-l5a004
  {:statement
   "Under conjugation by $U$, the Pauli expansion of $A = \\sum_P \\hat{a}(P) P$ transforms to $U A U^\\dagger = \\sum_P \\hat{a}(P) (U P U^\\dagger)$. Since $U P U^\\dagger$ spans the Pauli group bijectively (up to phases that don't affect coefficient magnitudes), the squared norm is preserved: $\\|U A U^\\dagger\\|_2^2 = \\|A\\|_2^2$. The Pauli spectral distribution of $U A U^\\dagger$ has $\\pi_{UAU^\\dagger}(Q) = \\pi_A(U^\\dagger Q U)$ where $Q = UPU^\\dagger$ for each $P$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "1f59c5236788292a",
   :display-order 4,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :algebraic-rewrite,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-l5a004,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{:1-l5a003}},
  :1-l5a005
  {:statement
   "Therefore $\\mathrm{Inf}(U A U^\\dagger) = \\sum_Q \\mathrm{wt}(Q) \\cdot \\pi_{UAU^\\dagger}(Q) = \\sum_P \\mathrm{wt}(UPU^\\dagger) \\cdot \\pi_A(P) = \\sum_P \\mathrm{wt}(P) \\cdot \\pi_A(P) = \\mathrm{Inf}(A)$, where the second-to-last equality uses $\\mathrm{wt}(UPU^\\dagger) = \\mathrm{wt}(P)$. QED.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "75ddacd9117d75f2",
   :display-order 5,
   :type :qed,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :qed,
